# Core (read first)
Layout: `playbook-*.mdc` = generic dev playbook (copyable to other projects). `project-*.mdc` = TravelAgency specifics (override the playbook where stated). Role subagents: `.cursor/agents/` (incl. `lead.md`, `architect.md`).

- Language: talk to the owner in Russian; agent-to-agent in English. Repo artifacts (commits, PRs, issues, comments, wiki, code comments): Russian, impersonal.
- Impersonal everywhere outside `.cursor/` and `AGENTS.md`: no AI/agent/bot/Cursor mentions, no role labels, no names, no `Co-authored-by` for bots. Write «принято решение», «добавлено», «проверено».
- No em dash (U+2014) in anything you write.
- Secrets: `playbook-security.mdc`. Never print, commit or paste one.
- Owner approval required for: server changes, deleting data, secrets, repo settings/access, history rewrite or force-push, spending money, important architecture decisions, and Dependabot docker and github-actions updates (including grouped updates that may contain majors). npm and NuGet Dependabot bumps, including majors, follow `playbook-git-pr.mdc` and do not need a separate yes when CI is green and nothing needs clarification. Everything else in your zone: no approval. Team approval requests go through the lead.
- Results over process: read only what the task needs, minimal diff, stop at acceptance criteria, no gold-plating. Report: outcome first with links, then only decisions/risks.

Load on demand:
| Rule | When |
|---|---|
| `playbook-git-pr.mdc` | any commit, PR, review, merge |
| `playbook-workflow.mdc` + `playbook-step-0N-*.mdc` | feature work (doc-driven steps 1-8) |
| `playbook-security.mdc` | always before push |
| `playbook-cloud-agents.mdc` | launching or accepting a cloud agent |
| `project-travelagency.mdc` | facts, stack, roles, merge order |
| `project-github-formats.mdc` | commit/PR/issue/comment text, board statuses |
| `project-wiki.mdc` | any wiki edit |
| `project-cursor-automations.mdc` | merge, PR review, or weekly audit (Cursor Automations comments) |
